# Queen Latifah Performs ‘U.N.I.T.Y.’ at Thanksgiving Day Parade

> 🎵 *Curated Music Story from Rolling Stone Official Publications*

### 📖 The Full Story

Fresh off her induction into the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame, Queen Latifah made an appearance at the Thanksgiving Day parade on Saturday.

The rap legend delivered her classic 1993 single “U.N.I.T.Y.” from atop NBC’s Peacock float; in addition to the performance, Latifah also served as a commentator during NBC’s coverage of the postponed parade.

Earlier this year, Queen Latifah also played a major role in another awards show, the American Music Awards, which she hosted . The awards show took place in Las Vegas in May and marked the first time Latifah had hosted it since 1995. Latifah also hosted America’s Block Party on the Fourth of July. That event featured performances by the Smashing Pumpkins and Chris Stapleton and took place in L.A.

